- The Like/star toggle is either hidden entirely for logged-out visitors, or clicking it routes to `/signup` — hiding it is simpler and more honest (a logged-out user liking something that isn't tied to any account is confusing), do that.
- Detail page `/marketplace/:presetId`: full `Preset` detail — description, `authorNotes`, a layer-breakdown visualization (same colored-dot-strip-per-layer approach as the My Presets cards, sized up), the `sampleRunId`'s backtest report rendered inline or linked (look up via `BACKTEST_RUNS.find(r => r.id === preset.sampleRunId)`, and render its `MetricCards` + `EquityChart` right on the page — you already have both components, just feed them this run's data), the full `reviews` array (author initials avatar, star rating, date, body), and "Sign up to clone" instead of "Clone."

### 6.2 Authenticated marketplace detail (`/app/marketplace/:presetId`)
Same content as the public detail page, but the action button is real: **"Clone to my bots"** calls the existing `forkPreset` action (same as the in-app list page's "Fork Graph" button) and routes to the new bot's builder. Add a **"Report"** link (small, muted, bottom of page) that opens a simple `Dialog` with a reason `Select` (Spam / Misleading performance claims / Inappropriate content / Other) and a `Textarea`, submitting just shows a `toast.success('Report submitted', "We'll review this within 48 hours.")` — there's no moderation backend to actually send this to, and that's fine, the point is the flow doesn't dead-end.

Update `app/app/marketplace/page.tsx`'s cards (already made clickable in Phase 4 §10) to point here, and add a proper **sort dropdown** (Select: Most forked / Highest rated / Newest / Price: low to high) plus a **price filter** (`Segmented`: All / Free / Paid) next to the existing category filter — the spec calls for both and neither exists on the current list page.

### 6.3 Publish flow (`/app/marketplace/publish/:botId`)
A 5-step wizard, same visual pattern as the onboarding flow's step indicator (reuse that top progress bar component). Guard the entry: if `bot.runIds.length === 0`, redirect straight to the bot's backtest page with a toast explaining "Run at least one backtest before publishing" — the spec requires a backtest as proof, so make that a hard gate, not just a copy suggestion.

