- **`/notifications`**: `NOTIFICATION_EVENTS` (7 event types) each rendered as a row with three `Switch`es — Email / In-app / Webhook — per the spec. Store this as `notificationChannels: Record<string, { email: boolean; inApp: boolean; webhook: boolean }>` in the store, seeded with sensible defaults (in-app on for everything, email on for the important ones, webhook off unless Pro plan — grey out/disable the webhook column entirely when `plan !== 'pro'`, matching `PLAN_COMPARISON`'s "Webhooks: Pro only" row).
- **`/api-keys`**: gated behind `plan === 'pro'` (show an `UpgradeNudge` instead of the content otherwise, matching the pattern already used elsewhere for plan-gated content). `API_KEYS` list — name, scope badge, prefix (masked, e.g. `ae_live_7f2a••••••`), created date, last used. "Generate new key" opens a `Dialog`: name field + scope `Select` (read / read+write), on submit generates a fake key string (`ae_live_` + a random hex chunk via `slugId`-style generation), shows it **once** in a copyable code block with a "you won't see this again" warning (standard API-key UX), then adds the masked version to the list. "Revoke" per row goes through `ConfirmDialog`.
- **`/danger-zone`**: this is account-level, distinct from the bot-level danger zone already in `SettingsTab` (leave that one alone — it's correctly scoped to a single bot). Two actions: **"Export all data"** — serialize the current `useWorkspace.getState()` and `useSession.getState()` (minus obviously-sensitive-looking fields, though nothing here is real) into one JSON object and trigger a `Blob` download named `aether-export-${date}.json` — this is a real, working export, not a stub. **"Delete account"** — a multi-step `ConfirmDialog` (or a small dedicated dialog with a type-to-confirm pattern: user must type the word `delete` into a field before the button enables — a nice, cheap bit of extra ceremony for the scariest action in the app), which on confirm calls `reset()` on both stores, clears `localStorage` keys, and routes to `/`.

Redirect the old routes: `app/app/settings/page.tsx` and `app/app/settings/profile/page.tsx` both become simple redirects to `/app/account/profile` (same one-line pattern already used for `app/app/billing/credits/page.tsx`), preserving any old bookmarks/links instead of breaking them. Update `components/app/app-topbar.tsx`'s `AccountMenu` links (`/app/settings/profile` → `/app/settings`) to point at `/app/account/profile` and `/app/account/security` respectively where it currently only offers one generic "Settings" link — split it into "Profile" and "Settings" (or just "Account") menu items now that there's a real multi-tab destination.

