## 12. Docs detail pages + Blog

### 12.1 `app/docs/[slug]/page.tsx`
Look up via `DOC_SECTIONS.find(d => d.slug === slug)`, `notFound()` if missing. Render `blocks` in order: `p` → paragraph, `h2`/`h3` → headings, `list` → `<ul>` of `items`, `code` → a `<pre>` block with monospace styling (match the dark-background treatment already used for the builder's console log and the live page's audit trail, for visual consistency across "terminal-styled" content), `note` → a callout box styled like the existing "What is a Strategy Backtest?" info box on the backtest config page (brand-tinted border + background + icon). Sidebar or top breadcrumb back to `/docs`, plus "reading time" and "category" shown same as the list card. A "Next guide" / "Previous guide" footer nav using array order within the same `category` is a nice, cheap addition.

### 12.2 `app/blog/page.tsx` + `app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`
`BLOG_POSTS` — list page is a simple card grid (title, excerpt, author, date, category badge, reading time), detail page renders... there's no `body`/`content` field on `BlogPost`, only `excerpt` — so the detail page shows the excerpt as a lead paragraph plus a clearly-labeled "Full post coming soon" notice, rather than fabricating body copy that doesn't exist in the data model. This is the one page in this entire phase where the honest answer is "the data model doesn't support a full article yet" — don't invent paragraphs of fake blog content to fill the space; a short real page beats a long fabricated one.

