## 13. Version restore page (`app/app/builder/[botId]/version/[versionId]/page.tsx`)

Found during the Phase 4 audit, not in the original non-goals list, but genuinely dead today: `components/builder/builder-toolbar.tsx`'s "Version history" menu already links each entry to `` /app/builder/${bot.id}/version/${v.id} ``, and this route has never existed.

Build it read-only by default: render the same `Canvas` component the live builder uses, but fed the historical snapshot instead of the live graph, with `LibraryPanel`, `Inspector`, and editing entirely absent — just the canvas, zoomed to fit, non-draggable (pass a prop through to disable dragging, or simplest, load the nodes/edges into a throwaway local `useState` instead of the `useBuilder` store so there's no accidental interaction with live editing state). A header bar: "Viewing version {label} · saved {date} · {note}" plus two buttons: **"Restore this version"** (through `ConfirmDialog`, since it overwrites the current graph — on confirm, calls `saveGraph` with this version's nodes/edges and routes to the live builder) and **"Back to current version"** (routes to `/app/builder/${botId}`).

**Data gap to fix first**: `BotVersion` (`mock/data.ts`) currently stores `label`/`createdAt`/`note`/`nodeCount` but **not** the actual `nodes`/`edges` snapshot — there's nothing to restore yet. Add `nodes: BotNode[]` and `edges: BotEdge[]` to the `BotVersion` interface, and update `snapshotVersion` in `lib/workspace-store.ts` (called today from the builder toolbar's rename handler and presumably elsewhere on save) to actually capture the graph at snapshot time, not just metadata about it.

